{"word":{"slug":"ol-ol16027027w","name":"Three Best Loved Barbara Cartlands","title":"Three Best Loved Barbara Cartlands","wordTypes":["word","bookSubmission"]},"bookSubmission":{"slug":"ol-ol16027027w","title":"Three Best Loved Barbara Cartlands","authorName":"Barbara Cartland","authorPubkey":null,"openLibraryId":"OL16027027W","coverUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6873822-L.jpg","pageCount":463,"publishYear":1975,"language":"eng","subjects":["Fiction, Romance, Historical","Love stories, fiction","Anthology","Love stories"],"blurb":"BEWITCHED: Saviya, a beautiful raven-haired, green-eyed gypsy girl, is nearly killed when she stumbles into the path of the Marquis of Ruckley's careening carriage. The accident turns out to be a stroke of luck for the Marquis, who has bet that he can pass off a common girl as a lady. What he hasn't wagered on is falling in love with his enchanting imposter!

A SWORD TO THE HEART tells of lovely Natalia Graystoke, penniless though titled, who knows that Lord Ranulf Colwall is the one men she can love. But on her wedding night, she overhears her husband say that he can never love any woman - all he desires is an heir for his vast estate. Desperate and afraid, she flees her new home, still hoping she has kindled some spark of affection that will bring him to her side.

THE GLITTERING LIGHTS is the story of young, willful Cassandra Sherburn, whose father has arranged her marriage to the Duke of Alchester, a man she hasn't seen since childhood. Horrified by the thought that the dashing young duke is marrying her for her money, she becomes determined to win him on her own merits. Fired by a scheme to capture his heart, she sets off for London masquerading as an actress.","format":"reference","fileUrl":null,"source":"openlibrary","submittedBy":null}}
